ous rounds but decided to bet 126 on the River. This indicates they likely have a pair of Queens, a Jack (giving them trips), or a better high card (like an Ace or King) which dominates your 5-high kicker.\n\nReason: You have no showdown value. Calling requires investing chips into a pot you will almost certainly lose. Raising is a reckless bluff given the opponent's river aggression suggests they finally made a hand. Folding is the safest and most statistically sound option to preserve your stack for a hand with actual winning potential.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
