d cards (K-8-5), and you lose to any King or a better Queen.\n\nA bet here is thin value; while you might get called by an 8 or 5, you risk folding out the hands you beat or getting raised by a random two pair or slow-played hand. Checking allows you to get to showdown cheaply and realize your equity without risking more chips on a marginal hand. Given the passive play, a check is the most prudent move to secure the likely win.\n\nReason: You have Second Pair with a weak kicker. The opponent's checks on the Flop and Turn indicate weakness (likely no King or strong Queen). Checking minimizes risk and secures a showdown where you are favored to win against lower pairs or air.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
